CrossChainTransfer_CctpxAdapter_Integration_Concrete_Test
├── when amount zero
│  └── it should revert with InvalidAmount
└── when amount non zero
   ├── when recipient zero
   │  └── it should revert with InvalidRecipient
   └── when recipient non zero
      ├── when minFinalityThreshold not fast or standard
      │  └── it should revert with InvalidFinalityThreshold
      └── when minFinalityThreshold fast or standard
         ├── when msg value above maxNativeFee
         │  └── it should revert with NativeFeeTooHigh
         └── when msg value at most maxNativeFee
            ├── when caller is not the route vault
            │  └── it should revert with RouteNotAllowed
            ├── when route is for another adapter
            │  └── it should revert with RouteNotAllowed
            ├── when route is for another token
            │  └── it should revert with RouteNotAllowed
            ├── when destination domain is not the route domain
            │  └── it should revert with RouteNotAllowed
            ├── when recipient is not the route recipient
            │  └── it should revert with RouteNotAllowed
            ├── when route pins an output token
            │  └── it should revert with RouteNotAllowed
            └── when route allowed
               ├── when msg value above quote total
               │  └── it should revert with IncorrectNativeFee
               ├── when msg value below quote total
               │  ├── given service cannot cover the shortfall
               │  │  └── it should revert in the service
               │  └── given service covers the shortfall from its own balance
               │     └── it should revert with IncorrectNativeFee
               └── when msg value equals quote total
                  ├── when reentered through token transfer hook
                  │  └── it should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall
                  ├── when msg value equals maxNativeFee
                  │  └── it should transfer
                  ├── given service holds ETH from earlier callers
                  │  └── it should transfer and leave the service balance unchanged
                  ├── given token manager pulls less than approved
                  │  ├── it should reset the token manager allowance to zero
                  │  └── it should leave the unpulled tokens in the adapter for rescue
                  └── when not reentered
                     ├── it should pull amount from the vault
                     ├── it should credit amount to the token manager
                     ├── it should forward tokenId amount and destination domain
                     ├── it should forward the recipient as its raw 20 bytes
                     ├── it should forward a zero destination caller
                     ├── it should forward minFinalityThreshold
                     ├── it should forward the signed quote with the vault as refund address
                     ├── it should not request a destination hook
                     ├── it should pay msg value as the fee
                     ├── it should reset the token manager allowance to zero
                     ├── it should leave zero token and zero ETH in the adapter
                     ├── it should emit AdapterAction
                     └── it should return amount
